Alpha Centauri’s recorded planets are **Proxima Centauri b** and **Proxima Centauri d**. The knowledge base records no moons for either, so none are identified as habitable. It describes Proxima Centauri b itself as orbiting in the habitable zone.

```sparql
PREFIX dbo: <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/>
PREFIX dbp: <http://dbpedia.org/property/>
PREFIX schema: <https://schema.org/>

SELECT DISTINCT ?planetName ?description WHERE {
  <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Alpha_Centauri> schema:hasPart ?binary .
  ?star dbp:star ?binary .
  ?planet a dbo:Planet ; dbp:star ?star ; schema:name ?planetName .
  OPTIONAL { ?planet schema:description ?description }
}
ORDER BY ?planetName
```

```sparql
SELECT DISTINCT ?s ?p ?o WHERE {
  ?s ?p ?o .
  FILTER(
    CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?s)), "moon") ||
    CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?p)), "moon") ||
    CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?o)), "moon") ||
    CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?o)), "habitable")
  )
}
ORDER BY ?s ?p ?o
```
